# Ciphertext file -> owner:group:mode[:format] of the decrypted file in /run.
# One line per ciphertext under /etc/smortress/secrets. scripts/sops-decrypt.sh
# fails closed on a missing ciphertext, an unlisted ciphertext, or a bad mode.
#
# format is optional:
#   yaml   the decrypted YAML is written verbatim (default)
#   value  the file's single top-level scalar is written, nothing else; a
#          restic --password-file cannot read a YAML document with a key
#
# healthchecks.yaml holds the single ping URL the freshness verifier uses; the
# whole YAML document is decryptable but only that one key is ever read.
#
# The two application secrets are single scalars because Podman secrets and the
# Immich `_FILE` variables need the bare value, not a YAML key. They stay
# root-only on purpose: smortress-app-secrets.service reads them as root and
# hands the value to each container at its own uid and mode.
# name                        uid   gid   mode  format
canary.yaml                   root  root  0400
cloudflared-tunnel.yaml       root  root  0400  value
restic-password.yaml          root  root  0400  value
r2-credentials.yaml           root  root  0400
healthchecks.yaml             root  root  0400
immich-db-password.yaml       root  root  0400  value
opdshelf-admin-password.yaml  root  root  0400  value
